qr_code: add explicit lifetimes for newer rustc elided-lifetime diagnostics

rustc has tightened its elided-lifetime-in-paths handling since this crate
(qr_code 2.0.0) was vendored; QrCode::iter and Parser::new both return a type
carrying a lifetime from an elided `&self`/`&[u8]` parameter without naming
it, which a newer rustc flags as an error rather than a warning under this
build's lint configuration.

Add the lifetime explicitly in both signatures. No behavioural change: this
is the same lifetime the compiler was already inferring, written out rather
than elided.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Yocto toolchain workaround for a vendored
Chromium third-party crate; not a Chromium or qr_code upstream change]

